## What I implemented

**`crates/inference-wllama/`** — the sole local inference engine per AMD-2. wllama3 is a TypeScript/WASM library that runs in the WebView, so the Rust crate wraps it through a `WllamaBridge` trait that Ring 3 (Tauri) implements; this crate owns every piece of behavior that can be carried out without crossing the language boundary.

| Module | What it does (all real, no stubs) |
|---|---|
| `gguf.rs` | Streams the file once, checks `ModelFormat::Gguf`, `BackendKind::LocalLm` support, well-formed SHA-256, the `0x46554747` magic at offset 0, total size, and SHA-256 against `ModelManifest.artifact_sha256` |
| `prompt.rs` | Folds system prompt + numbered evidence block + coerces unknown roles to `"user"`, rejects NUL bytes, replaces empty `messages` with a single empty user turn |
| `session.rs` | Implements `InferenceSession`: emits `CitationMarker`s for evidence at stream start, then forwards bridge `Delta`/`Usage`/`Done`/`Failed` events as `TextDelta`/`Usage`/`Completed`/`Err`. Real cancellation via per-request registry + `bridge.abort`. Real `close` via `bridge.unload` |
| `backend.rs` | `WllamaInferenceBackend` (`InferenceBackend`: descriptor, health via `bridge.probe`, `validate_model`, `open_session` with re-verification + UUID session id) and `WllamaEmbeddingBackend` (`EmbeddingBackend`: lazy `ensure_loaded`, `embed` with optional L2 normalization, dimensionality/order invariants) |
| `bridge.rs` | The IPC trait Ring 3 wires to Tauri WebView eval — typed `WllamaLoadParams`, `WllamaChatParams`, `WllamaStreamEvent`, `WllamaProbe`, etc. |
| `ipc.rs` / `clock.rs` | JSON IPC shapes + wall-clock helper for `BackendHealth.checked_at_ms` |

## `cargo check -p inference-wllama` result

- **My crate is clean.** When temporarily isolating it from the documented `ports/src/platform.rs` defect (the ARCH-02 task in flight — explicitly called out in the task description as "not yours"), `cargo check --locked -p inference-wllama` finishes with **zero errors, zero warnings**, and `cargo test --locked -p inference-wllama` passes **21/21** tests (5 unit suites + 7 integration tests covering exact stream ordering, cancel→abort, close→unload, embedding normalization paths, GGUF magic, manifest-backed SHA-256/size checks).
- **At workspace baseline**, the check halts at `ports` because `ports/src/platform.rs` references five types (`PlatformCapabilityReport`, `PlatformError`, `PlatformStorageRoot`, `PowerState`, `NetworkState`) that are not defined — the known parallel-known defect. `ports/` was temporarily stubbed **only** for my crate's verification, then restored byte-for-byte (`git status` shows no diff in `crates/ports/`).
